  "_bnKinds_doc": "WHAT A BATTALION IS MADE OF — companies and the slots inside them. A slot is either a FIELDABLE unit type, a `roster` naming an element above, or a `flight` (airframes plus a crew roster repeated per airframe). `plts` is shorthand for n numbered platoons of one type. A COMBINED ARMS BATTALION is three maneuver companies and it is NOT symmetrical: an ABCT fields two armor-heavy CABs (two tank companies, one mech) and one infantry-heavy (two mech, one tank) — the brigade's balance comes from the mix across battalions. The FORWARD SUPPORT COMPANY is assigned to the BSB and attached forward to a CAB, so it lives in the BSB and `tfCos` attaches it, exactly as the real paperwork runs.",
